{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the high priest among his brethren.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): after He imposed restrictions upon the ordinary priest and forbade him corpse-impurity except for known dead, and forbade him also the disqualified women — a zonah and a chalalah and a divorcee — except for a widow, He now added and imposed further restrictions upon the high priest, who is sanctified and inward, more specially designated for the service of HaShem — he shall not depart from the sanctuary — so that it is forbidden to him to become impure through any corpse in the world, even for his father and for his mother, and so that he is likewise forbidden in all women except a fit virgin. And the reason for this is so that she be drawn after his knowledge and his will, and the high priest must be more tightly bound in the matter of intercourse; therefore a woman who had previously been accustomed to another man was forbidden to him, lest she draw him after her own knowledge." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> 'And the high priest among his brethren' — that he should be greater than his brethren in five things: in beauty, in strength, in wealth, in wisdom, in honor. And if he lacks these, his brethren the priests enrich him, as it says: ״והכהן הגדול מאחיו״ — make him great from among his brethren. And there was an incident with Pinchas the stonemason: they anointed him as high priest, and his brethren the priests went out and saw him hewing stones, and they filled the quarry before him with gold dinars." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> the high priest — it is known who his counterpart is, and I have already mentioned this in the section of צו. And the deputy (sagan) was at his right and the head of the father's house at his left, in counterpart to the seraphim; and this is what the angel said to Joshua the high priest (Zechariah 3): ״ונתתי לך מהלכים״ and so on — he hinted to him his place and his counterpart. And Jonathan translated: 'among the seraphim of these,' from what is written (Isaiah 6): ״שרפים עומדים ממעל לו״." "<b>And they said</b> in tractate Yoma, chapter הממונה: the sagan at his right and the head of the father's house at his left. And furthermore it was taught in a baraita: three walking on the road — the teacher in the middle, the elder at his right, and the younger at his left. And so we find with the three angels who came to Abraham: Michael in the middle, Gabriel at his right, Raphael at his left." "<b>And if</b> you merit, you will understand that for this reason Scripture employed this expression regarding him, 'the high priest,' in the manner of what is written (Deuteronomy 11): ״את כל מעשה ה' הגדול״ and so on — for the service of the high priest is unto the Great Name. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory said in tractate Horayot, chapter כהן משיח: (Leviticus 21) ״את ראשו לא יפרע ובגדיו לא יפרום״ — 'he shall not rend at all; words of R. Yehudah. R. Shimon says: he does not rend above, but he rends below,' that is, underneath his garments, not in the upper garment, as is the law of tearing for an ordinary priest and for the rest of Israel. And this comes to hint that the tearing is only for one who is beneath him, namely the ordinary priest; therefore the high priest rends below, because in his counterpart there is no descent but only ascent, upward and upward, to the infinite. And the term פרימה means tearing, as in its Aramaic translation יבזע."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:44.771843790Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}